+## Recovery
+
+Protect the store before risky operations and recover from a known-good
+snapshot when needed:
+
+```sh
+harnie backup <path>
+```
+
+`harnie backup <path>` writes a consistent SQLite snapshot of the live store
+and creates the backup file with owner-read/write permissions (`0600`).
+
+```sh
+harnie restore <path> --force
+```
+
+`harnie restore <path> --force` validates the backup file and, if it is a
+valid SQLite store, overwrites the live store with it. Restore has **no undo**:
+a bad backup replaces the live store, so keep recent backups and verify one
+before forcing the restore.

